We are given a bicyclic system: (1S,4R)-2-vinyl-2-azabicyclo[2.2.1]hept-5-ene.  
The Cope rearrangement is a [3,3]-sigmatropic rearrangement. Here, the vinyl group is attached to the nitrogen, and the system contains a double bond in the bridge. The rearrangement will involve the vinyl and the double bond in the ring, forming a new ring system.

Drawing the structure:  
The bicyclic system has a nitrogen at position 2, with a vinyl substituent. The [2.2.1] hept-5-ene means there is a double bond between C5 and C6. The Cope rearrangement will connect the vinyl to the other end of the diene system, expanding the ring.

After rearrangement, the product is a fused cyclopenta[c]pyridine system. The stereochemistry (1S,4R) influences which tetrahydro isomer forms. The correct product from the given options is the one with the double bond in the 7,7a position relative to the pyridine ring, which corresponds to **4,4a,7,7a-tetrahydro-1H-cyclopenta[c]pyridine**.

Thus the answer is D.

Answer: D
