Set equal: 5(12-b) = 19b → 60 - 5b = 19b → 60 = 24b → b = 60/24 = 5/2 = 2.5.

But earlier from circle: a²+b²=36 → a² = 36 - (2.5)² = 36 - 6.25 = 29.75 = 119/4. So a = √(119)/2. Then rectangle area = (2a)(2b) = 4ab = 4*(√119/2)*(5/2) = 4*(5√119/4) = 5√119. That’s not rational m/n. So something off: b from area equality gave b=2.5, but diagram b≈3.3166. So maybe rectangle not centered? Let’s re-evaluate.

