**Step 5 – Solve for a,b from area equality and circle**

Area(DGF) = 5(12-b) (since GF horizontal length 2a, height 12-b). Actually GF from (-a,b) to (a,b) length = 2a. So area = (1/2)*(2a)*(12-b) = a(12-b).

Area(CHG): GH vertical from (-a,-b) to (-a,b) length = 2b. Horizontal distance from C(-24,0) to line x=-a is 24-a (since -24 to -a is a-(-24)? Actually distance = | -a - (-24) | = 24 - a). So area = (1/2)*(2b)*(24-a) = b(24-a).

