Answer: <line number or comma-separated line numbers>
QUESTION_PROMPT_END
MODEL_OUTPUT_BEGIN bytes=290
The bug is introduced at line 8. The pointer `tp` is decremented before any bytes have been written to `tmp`, so `colonp` points to one byte before the start of `tmp`. This causes an out-of-bounds write when `memmove` and `memset` are later used with `colonp` as the destination.

